  "description": "All that you need to know about MEDHA 2026 Focus Area: This is an AI-focused, software-only hackathon. All solutions must be software-based and must incorporate Artificial Intelligence or Machine Learning at their core. Possible domains include (but are not limited to): Natural Language Processing & Generative AI Computer Vision & Image Recognition Predictive Analytics & Data Intelligence AI for Healthcare & Assistive Tech AI for Sustainability & Smart Systems AI in Cybersecurity Autonomous Systems & Decision Making Problem Statements: Problem statements will not be released at the time of registration. They will be made available to all participants after the closing of registrations. Teams should prepare their AI/software foundations before the reveal. Important Notes & Policies: No travel or accommodation will be provided. Participants must manage their own arrangements. Shortlisted teams must be physically present for the final offline round. Team changes are not allowed without prior approval. Participants must maintain professional conduct. Misconduct may lead to disqualification. Decisions of judges and organizers will be final and binding.",
